{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "מיסרך", :translit "meyasercha", :gloss "He chastises you"} {:he "תגין על המ\"ם", :translit "tagin al ha-mem", :gloss "tags on the mem"} {:he "שהנשמה נוצרה במ' יום", :translit "she-haneshamah nutzrah be-mem yom", :gloss "that the soul was created in forty days"} {:he "והתורה נתנה במ' יום", :translit "ve-hatorah nitnah be-mem yom", :gloss "and the Torah was given in forty days"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Decorative tagin drawn on the closed mem of מיסרך, signaling the thematic link between the two sets of forty days."}], :frame {:text "The number forty carries structural weight in rabbinic chronology: Moses spent forty days on Mount Sinai to receive the Torah (Deuteronomy 9:9, 9:18, 10:10), and the Talmud states that a male fetus is formed in forty days (Berakhot 60a; see also Talmud Yerushalmi Yevamot 4:5 regarding embryo formation). Ba'al HaTurim compresses these into a wordplay: the mem of מיסרך, whose numerical value is forty, ties the giving of the Torah to the creation of the soul, so that neglect of Torah warrants the forfeiture of soul.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 9:9" "Deuteronomy 9:18" "Deuteronomy 10:10" "Berakhot 60a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Decorative tagin drawn on the closed mem of מיסרך, signaling the thematic link between the two sets of forty days.", :by :selah, :ran? false}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 8, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:35:12.563436473Z", :model "glm-5.2"}